# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Any .env anywhere. deployment/compose/.env is the one this repository still
# writes: Compose reads it from the compose file's own directory, so it cannot
# move into .local/. The pattern stays broad so a stray one is never committable.
.env

# OpenTofu working directories and local state. Provider locks stay committed.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Contributor-local configuration: credentials, model entries, and a hand-applied
# Kubernetes Secret. `./make setup local` creates it from the committed
# templates and `./make doctor` reports on it. Nothing in it is ever committed.
/.local/

# End-to-end suite evidence: traces, screenshots, and the note saying what ran.
# `./make e2e` clears and rewrites it every run.
/.artifacts/

# Release artifacts. Both are generated: dist/ by GoReleaser, NOTICE-THIRD-PARTY
# by the `./make release notices` task during the release build.
/dist/
/NOTICE-THIRD-PARTY

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Agent/assistant local working directories
.claude/
.cursor/

# Internal task-note and scratch area used by the /vibe workflow.
# Published documentation lives in docs/.
.vibe/
# Built binaries. `./make build` writes to bin/; a bare `go build ./cmd/<x>`
# writes <x> to the repository root instead, so every cmd package is listed
# here whether or not ./make ever produces it. Do not ignore cmd/* source.
/bin/
/buildmax
/buildmax-desktop
/buildmax-server
/buildmax-worker
/buildmax-eval
/local-test-mcp-server
/mk

testing-sandbox/
testing-workspaces/

# Scratch directory the /smoke skill writes to. It cleans up after itself; this
# line is here so an interrupted run does not leave untracked files behind.
/smoke-test-tmp/

# Server/portal workspace dirs created by tests or local runs when WorkspacesDir is unset
internal/server/**/testing-workspaces/
internal/server/**/ws-1/
internal/server/**/ws1/

# Shared GUI package (React / Node)
gui/node_modules/
gui/dist/
gui/*.tsbuildinfo

# Portal (React / Node)
portal/node_modules/
portal/dist/
portal/*.tsbuildinfo

# Desktop app (Wails) — frontend in desktop/frontend (React + Vite).
# Vite writes its bundle to desktop/dist, not desktop/frontend/dist, so that
# desktop/assets_embed.go can embed it: desktop/frontend is a separate Go module
# and //go:embed cannot cross a module boundary.
cmd/buildmax-desktop/build/
desktop/dist/
desktop/frontend/wailsjs/
desktop/frontend/node_modules/
desktop/frontend/.env
desktop/frontend/.env.*
desktop/frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
desktop/frontend/package.json.md5

/eval-results

# The Harbor adapter under evaluation/harbor is the repository's only Python,
# and running its tests or the harness itself leaves these behind.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
evaluation/harbor/.venv/
# Written by `uv run` alongside that venv. The adapter's dependency is pinned
# exactly in pins.json and pyproject.toml, which is what a run is reproduced
# from; this file is a local resolution artifact of running its tests.
evaluation/harbor/uv.lock
evaluation/harbor/*.egg-info/
